I’ll inspect the diffraction data and metadata first, then use the available indexing/search and GSAS-II tooling to identify phases, refine the multiphase model, and validate that every requested artifact is internally consistent.

The chemistry suggests a Ba–W–O reaction system, but the 400 °C treatment makes residual precursors or intermediates plausible. I’m now mapping the peak set and checking which local crystallographic databases and refinement interfaces are available before committing to phase identities.

The peak positions now separate cleanly into two precursor signatures: monoclinic WO₃ gives the shifted 23.43/23.90/24.66° triplet, while orthorhombic BaCO₃ accounts for the 24.21° line and its full higher-angle series. The common ≈+0.3° displacement is instrumental/specimen-position related; I’ll model that in GSAS-II rather than distorting either lattice. I’m also testing whether any BaWO₄ contribution is statistically supported.

The first full refinements already give a good two-phase fit (about 8% weighted profile R-factor), with both phases refining to sensible room-temperature cells. I’m comparing symmetry-equivalent and alternative WO₃ models in parallel, because choosing the correct WO₃ polymorph matters more here than squeezing the profile with extra empirical parameters.

Both precursor phases are independently required: either one alone leaves a weighted profile R-factor near 25–27%, versus ~7.3% together. A trace BaWO₄ scale is also statistically positive in a controlled test, so I’m now refining that candidate conservatively with its cell fixed; this avoids mistaking an unstable trace-phase cell refinement for evidence of a real product.

The conservative three-phase model is holding: BaCO₃ and WO₃ dominate, while scheelite BaWO₄ refines near 0.6 wt% and remains significant when all other parameters are reoptimized. Competing Ba–W oxides only fit at sub-0.2 wt% levels comparable to residual-model bias, so I’m excluding those rather than overfitting. The final clean project and exports are being regenerated from the raw pattern now.

